  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inst&apos;l Capacity Building for Integration of Indigenous Knowledge</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at building local capacity for the sustainable integration of IK in development. The pillars of sucessful integration are a well defined and actionable national strategy, a national coordination  mechanism, local capacity to capture, store, exchange and develop IK, and  regional information exchange. The project has the following five major components: 1. I dentification of key priority issues, training needs, and an action framework for the implementation of the IK strategy. 2. A wider participatory review in 8 selected districts from a wider cross section of stakeholders and the community level to explore the issues sorrounding the adoption and use of IK in community development. 3. Refine and officially launch the national program of action for integration of IK into priority sectors of rural development. 4. Coordinate training of communities, ministries and other actors in advocacy of IK 5. Strengthening of UNCST as  a coordinating unit for IK.</narrative>
  </description>
